From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 12:24:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: do not write a source MAC into an L2B PPE entry

airoha_set_ppe_mac() casts the l2 block of every entry up to the
DS-Lite type to struct airoha_foe_mac_info. That includes the bridge
(L2B) type, whose l2 block has only the 16 common bytes and is
followed by meter and tunnel_mtu. For a bridge entry the function
wrote the low 16 bits of the source MAC into tunnel_mtu and a PPPoE
session id into meter.

An L2B entry has no source MAC to program, because the MAC pair is a
key field. The vendor l2b bind fix added this rule to
airoha_ppe_foe_entry_prepare() and left the vendor function without
it. The function now writes the destination MAC only for a bridge
entry. This affects every bridged flow that the vendor bind paths
offload.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_ppe.c |    7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_ppe.c
@@ -934,6 +934,13 @@ int airoha_set_ppe_mac(struct airoha_foe
 	}
 	l2->dest_mac_hi = get_unaligned_be32(dst_mac);
 	l2->dest_mac_lo = get_unaligned_be16(dst_mac + 4);
+
+	/* The l2 block of an L2B entry has 16 bytes, so the cast below would
+	 * write over meter and tunnel_mtu. The MAC pair is a key field there.
+	 */
+	if (type == PPE_PKT_TYPE_BRIDGE)
+		return 0;
+
 	if (type <= PPE_PKT_TYPE_IPV4_DSLITE) {
 		struct airoha_foe_mac_info *mac_info;
 		mac_info = (struct airoha_foe_mac_info *)l2;
